leted","toolCallId":"call_NYCBxHuKVyHIV1qONUwt9VBm","sessionId":"4a135ea5-3967-4256-a28b-a2cb316c94af","seq":4526,"startedSeq":4520,"endedSeq":4526,"timestamp":"1788660918Z","raw":{"_meta":{"goldBandConversation":{"branchId":"root","toolName":"PowerShell","toolDetailAvailable":false}}}},{"id":"assistant-thought-root-resp_0aa6e6df14be0779016a9cccc06c9c87d08a66cfa981a95eaa","kind":"thoughtDelta","sessionId":"4a135ea5-3967-4256-a28b-a2cb316c94af","seq":4537,"startedSeq":4528,"endedSeq":4537,"timestamp":"1788660933Z","raw":{"_meta":{"goldBandConversation":{"branchId":"root","toolName":null,"toolDetailAvailable":false}}},"content":"**Planning native library extraction in image build**\n**Implementing native library extraction and volume ownership fix**\n**Evaluating volume permission strategies**\n**Refining volume naming and ownership approach**\n**Confirming /tmp requirements for nginx**\n**Planning Dockerfile runtime verification**\n**Designing Docker build smoke test with timeout**\n**Considering Docker build test task execution**\n**Planning native library permissions and runtime smoke tests**\n**Designing Dockerfile native library extraction and healthcheck strategy**"},{"id":"assistant-message-root-resp_0aa6e6df14be0779016a9cccc06c9c87d08a66cfa981a95eaa","kind":"textDelta","sessionId":"4a135ea5-3967-4256-a28b-a2cb316c94af","seq":4644,"startedSeq":4538,"endedSeq":4644,"timestamp":"1788660970Z","raw":{"_meta":{"goldBandConversation":{"branchId":"root","toolName":null,"toolDetailAvailable":false}}},"content":"The root cause is precise: `/tmp` is intentionally mounted `noexec`, so Xerial can find the embedded `.so` but cannot load the extracted copy; its terminal exception is therefore misleading. The correct boundary is to extract the pinned Linux native into the immutable image and point Xerial there, while keeping `/tmp` non-executable. Separately, the one-click deployment will use a Compose-owned named metadata volume initialized with UID 10001 ownership, and Ngin